Add <stddef.h> to the emscripten platform header.

zenoh-pico/include/zenoh-pico/system/common/platform.h declares a dozen
prototypes taking size_t, but includes only <stdbool.h> and <stdint.h>. Every
other platform gets size_t transitively: platform.h lines 30-40 pull in the
POSIX/Windows/Zephyr socket headers for ZENOH_LINUX, ZENOH_MACOS, ZENOH_BSD,
ZENOH_WINDOWS and ZENOH_ZEPHYR. There is no such branch for ZENOH_EMSCRIPTEN.

The emscripten platform header only includes <pthread.h> -- which would have
supplied size_t -- under Z_FEATURE_MULTI_THREAD == 1. We build single-threaded
on purpose (threads under emcc mean SharedArrayBuffer, which means the page
needs COOP/COEP headers), so nothing defines size_t and the library does not
compile:

    platform.h:136:31: error: unknown type name 'size_t'

Still present on 1.10.1, so this is not fixed by moving the pin. Upstreamable
as-is.

--- a/include/zenoh-pico/system/platform/emscripten.h
+++ b/include/zenoh-pico/system/platform/emscripten.h
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 #ifndef ZENOH_PICO_SYSTEM_WASM_TYPES_H
 #define ZENOH_PICO_SYSTEM_WASM_TYPES_H
 
+#include <stddef.h>
 #include <stdint.h>
 
 #include "zenoh-pico/config.h"
